/* book exam traps: Sign of skew. With δ = capture arrival − launch arrival, positive δ relaxes setup (T + δ) and tightens hold (th + δ). State the definition before writing either check. | Treating jitter like skew. Skew is constant and can help one check; jitter varies from cycle to cycle, appears as 2tjit and never helps. | Fixing a hold failure by slowing the clock. T is not in the hold check; add delay to the short path or reduce the skew. | Calling plesiochronous clocks mesochronous. Mesochronous means the same frequency with a fixed phase offset; plesiochronous frequencies differ slightly, so the phase keeps drifting. | Drawing a C-element as an AND gate. It holds its output while the inputs disagree; an AND gate does not. */
